      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.0600$ lies between. These numbers are $0.0594$ and $0.0606.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.0594 & <0.0600<0.0606\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.56) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.55).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-1.56+(-1.55)}{2}=-1.555.\n$$",
